{
 "schema": "kake-link-preview-matrix-v1",
 "round": 34,
 "tool": "scripts/link_preview_audit.py",
 "invocation": "python3 -B scripts/link_preview_audit.py --manifest <dir>/manifest.json   (cases with argv run that argv instead; cwd is the case directory)",
 "interface": [
  "stdout: one JSON object {verdict, pagesChecked, findings:[{id, reason, page, property}]} for exits 0, 1 and 2; exit 64 needs no JSON",
  "exit 0 verdict clean (no findings); exit 1 verdict failed-policy (policy findings only); exit 2 verdict could-not-evaluate (any input finding; then only input findings are reported, reasons input_invalid or page_unreadable); exit 64 usage (missing --manifest, unknown argument)",
  "manifest v1: {version:1, pages:[{file: relative path inside the manifest directory, url: absolute http(s) page URL}]} with non-empty pages; a file path that resolves outside the manifest directory is input_invalid; a listed file that cannot be read as UTF-8 is page_unreadable",
  "an Open Graph property is a <meta> element whose property attribute equals the name exactly (og:title, og:type, og:image, og:url) and whose content attribute is non-empty after stripping ASCII whitespace; name= attributes do not count",
  "policy findings: og_required_missing (property = the missing one of og:title, og:type, og:image, og:url; S067), og_type_multiple (more than one og:type element; S068), og_url_not_absolute (og:url value is not an absolute http or https URL with a host), og_url_not_canonical (og:url absolute, a <link rel=canonical href> exists, and og:url differs from that href resolved against the page URL; first canonical link wins; exact string comparison after stripping ASCII whitespace; S067, S068)",
  "findings are compared on the keys the expected findings carry (reason and property for policy findings; reason for input findings), as a sorted multiset"
 ],
 "comparison": "per case: exit equal; for exit 0/1/2 the verdict equal and the projected findings equal as sorted multisets; exit 64 compares exit only",
 "cases": [
